              "title": "Indirect dependency on concrete TTYBridge with no abstraction",
              "issue": "LogViewerView accesses TTYBridge transitively through SessionManager (`sessionManager?.bridge(for: agent.pid)`) and then calls concrete methods (`bridge?.sendRaw`, `bridge?.send`, `bridge?.detach`, `bridge?.isAttached`, `bridge?.onActivity`) at lines 295, 985, 999–1000, 1014, 1078, 1080, 1109, 1123, 1186, and 421–423. There is no protocol abstraction over TTYBridge, so the view cannot be exercised against a substitute that simulates PTY input/output without instantiating the real TTYBridge.",
              "impact": "Behavior that depends on PTY interaction (permission prompts, plan approval, ask-user prompts, send-input) cannot be unit-tested or extended without modifying LogViewerView. Adding a new transport (e.g. mock bridge, network bridge) requires source changes here rather than substitution.",
              "rule_source": "OCP-2 — 1+ untestable INDIRECT dependency → SEVERE"
            },
