              "id": "ocp-002",
              "severity": "MINOR",
              "metric": "OCP-1",
              "line_start": 217,
              "line_end": 218,
              "title": "DIRECT dependency on concrete AppSettings and SessionManager without protocol abstraction",
              "issue": "`settings: AppSettings` (line 217) and `sessionManager: SessionManager?` (line 218) are typed as concrete classes rather than as protocols. The view also reads multiple AppSettings flags (`settings.displayMode`, `settings.maxVisibleLogMessages`, `settings.expandThinking`, `settings.expandTools`) and mutates SessionManager state (`sessionManager?.sessions.removeValue(forKey: agent.pid)` at line 296). Replacing these with substitutes requires concrete instances, not contract-defined fakes.",
              "impact": "The view is closed against new settings/session-manager implementations; any extension requires modifying LogViewerView. Two testable DIRECT INJECTED concretes meet the MINOR threshold (0 sealed, 2 testable DIRECT).",
              "rule_source": "OCP-2 — 0 sealed points, 2 testable DIRECT INJECTED dependencies → MINOR"
            }
